# Neo Filter parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoFilter
namespace NeoBuzz.Filter
class NeoFilterMachine
summary Stereo resonant filter effect with Neo Poly's filters: the ladder (low-pass 24 or 12 dB/oct) and the state-variable filter (low-pass, band-pass, high-pass, notch, peak; 12 or 24 dB/oct), cutoff in Hz, resonance as Q up to self-oscillation that stays bounded, drive (soft saturation, oversampled), an envelope follower (attack, release, sensitivity, ± octaves) and an LFO (free or synced to the tempo, seven shapes, stereo phase, locked to the song or restarted by the input) both moving the cutoff, dry/wet mix and output. Zero latency; at Mix 0 % it passes the input bit for bit. Use it for filter sweeps, auto-wah, dub high-pass and low-pass moves, resonant tones and tempo-synced movement.

group Filter
Type      "Type"            0 6     0     enum Ladder_24 Ladder_12 SVF_LP SVF_BP SVF_HP SVF_Notch SVF_Peak | Ladder: Neo Poly's transistor ladder, low-pass 24 or 12 dB/oct (resonance thins the lows, as a ladder does); SVF: the state-variable filter's low-pass, band-pass, high-pass, notch or peak (unity on both sides, a peak of 2Q at the cutoff)
    how Chooses the filter: a 24 or 12 dB per octave ladder low-pass, or a state-variable low-pass, band-pass, high-pass, notch or peak.
    sound The ladder sounds warm and thick, low-pass types remove highs, band-pass and high-pass thin the sound, notch and peak carve or boost one spot.
Slope     "Slope"           0 1     0     enum 12_dB/oct 24_dB/oct      | SVF low-pass, band-pass, high-pass and notch: one section (12 dB/oct) or two alike in series (24 dB/oct, the resonance's peak doubled in dB). The ladder and the peak ignore it
    how Chooses a 12 or 24 dB per octave slope for the state-variable low-pass, band-pass, high-pass and notch (the ladder and peak ignore it).
    sound 24 dB per octave cuts more sharply, so the filtered range disappears faster; 12 dB is gentler and more natural.
Cutoff    "Cutoff"          0 10000 6667  freq 20 20000                 | Cutoff frequency (the ladder's stages, the SVF's centre): where the resonance peaks and the filter self-oscillates
    how Sets the filter's frequency, from 20 Hz to 20 kHz: the corner, or the centre for band-pass, notch and peak.
    sound Sweeping it makes the sound darker or brighter, or moves the thin band you hear.
Resonance "Resonance"       0 1000  66    exp 0.5 100 2                 | Resonance as the Q of the filter's resonant poles: 0.5 none, 0.71 flat (Butterworth), 2–5 a bump, 10 and up a whistle; at its top the filter self-oscillates, at a bounded level
    how Boosts the region around the cutoff by raising Q from 0.5 to 100.
    sound Low values sound plain, middle values add a bump, high values whistle and eventually ring on their own.
Drive     "Drive"           0 240   0     lin 0 24 dB 1                 | Soft saturation before the filter, oversampled: quiet signals pass as they are, louder ones bend from −Drive dBFS; 0 dB is clean
    how Adds up to 24 dB of soft saturation before the filter.
    sound More drive thickens and warms the sound, and makes the resonance bite harder.
group Envelope
EnvAmount "Env amount"      0 1200  600   lin -6 6 oct 2                | How far the input's envelope moves the cutoff, in octaves at full envelope (negative: down)
    how Sets how far the input's loudness moves the cutoff, from -6 to +6 octaves.
    sound Positive values open the filter on loud notes for a wah or plucky sweep; negative values close it.
EnvSens   "Env sensitivity" 0 480   120   lin -12 36 dB 1               | Gain on the detected level: the envelope is full when the input's peak reaches −Sensitivity dBFS
    how Sets how sensitive the envelope is, from -12 to +36 dB.
    sound Higher values make even quiet input sweep the filter fully; lower values need louder playing.
EnvAttack "Env attack"      0 1000  459   time 0.0001 0.5               | Envelope follower attack: the time constant of its rise (63 % of a step)
    how Sets how fast the envelope rises when the input gets louder, from 0.1 ms to 0.5 s.
    sound Fast attacks snap the filter open on every hit; slow ones make a gradual swell.
EnvRelease "Env release"    0 1000  588   time 0.001 5                  | Envelope follower release: the time constant of its fall (to 37 %)
    how Sets how fast the envelope falls when the input gets quieter, from 1 ms to 5 s.
    sound Short releases give a quick, bouncy wah; long ones let the filter glide slowly closed.
group LFO
LfoRate   "LFO rate"        0 1000  489   freq 0.01 30                  | LFO speed when LFO sync is Free
    how Sets the LFO's speed, from 0.01 to 30 Hz, when LFO sync is Free.
    sound Slow rates make gentle sweeps over seconds, fast rates make wobbles and tremolo-like movement.
LfoSync   "LFO sync"        0 18    0     enum Free 1/32 1/16T 1/16 1/16D 1/8T 1/8 1/8D 1/4T 1/4 1/4D 1/2T 1/2 1/2D 1_bar 2_bars 4_bars 8_bars 16_bars | One LFO cycle per note value of the song's tempo (T triplet, D dotted); Free: LFO rate
    how Locks one LFO cycle to a note value of the song's tempo, from 1/32 to 16 bars, or leaves it Free.
    sound The movement stays in time with the music, so sweeps land on the beat.
LfoShape  "LFO shape"       0 6     0     enum Sine Triangle Saw_up Saw_down Square S&H Smooth_random | LFO waveform (S&H: a random step per cycle; Smooth random: random points joined smoothly)
    how Chooses the LFO's waveform: sine, triangle, saw up, saw down, square, stepped random or smooth random.
    sound Sine and triangle sweep smoothly, saws ramp, square flips between two tones, random shapes wander.
LfoDepth  "LFO depth"       0 400   0     lin 0 4 oct 2                 | How far the LFO moves the cutoff either way, in octaves
    how Sets how far the LFO moves the cutoff either way, from 0 to 4 octaves.
    sound Small depths add subtle movement; large ones sweep the whole sound open and shut.
LfoSpread "LFO spread"      0 180   0     lin 0 180 ° 0                 | The right channel's LFO phase against the left's: 0° both alike, 90° in quadrature, 180° opposite
    how Offsets the right channel's LFO phase from the left's, from 0 to 180 degrees.
    sound At 0 degrees both sides move together; wider offsets make the sweep travel across the stereo field.
LfoRetrig "LFO retrig"      0 2     1     enum Free Song Env            | Free: the LFO runs on; Song: its phase follows the song's position while it plays (the same sweep on every pass and render); Env: it restarts at LFO phase when the input's envelope rises past half
    how Chooses when the LFO restarts: Free runs on, Song follows the song position, Env restarts on each rising input.
    sound Song repeats the same sweep on every pass; Env restarts the sweep on every hit.
LfoPhase  "LFO phase"       0 360   0     lin 0 360 ° 0                 | The LFO's phase at the song's start (Song) or where it restarts (Env)
    how Sets the LFO's starting phase, from 0 to 360 degrees, at the start of the song or at each restart.
    sound It decides where in the sweep each pass begins, for example starting dark or starting bright.
group Output
Mix       "Mix"             0 1000  1000  pct                           | Dry against filtered (a crossfade): 100 % only the filter
    how Blends the dry signal with the filtered signal.
    sound Lower values keep the original sound and add the filter as an accent; 100 % is only the filter.
Output    "Output"          0 480   240   db -24 24                     | Output gain, −24 … +24 dB in 0.1 dB steps
    how Adds -24 to +24 dB of gain after the filter.
    sound It restores the level lost to filtering, or keeps resonant peaks in check.
